00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:05.680
Imagine you bought shares of a US growth stock

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:09.940
inside your TFSA last month at $48.50.

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:12.500
The order filled cleanly,

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:15.700
yet you later discover the 15% withholding tax

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:17.320
on any future dividends

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.660
quietly reduces the compounding power

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:21.460
you thought was fully tax-free.

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:24.780
TFSA's shield Canadian source income

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:26.560
and capital gains completely,

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:29.760
but US dividends still face that withholding

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.860
unless held through a Canadian listed ETF wrapper

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:35.160
that avoids direct US exposure.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:38.180
Most retail investors do not realize

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:41.660
contribution room resets only on January 1st

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:43.400
and that over-contributions trigger

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:46.160
a 1% per month penalty until withdrawn.

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:50.000
Professionals always verify the exact unused room

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:52.280
on the CRA's My Account Portal

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:53.800
before any large purchase

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:56.160
rather than relying on brokerage estimates.

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:59.080
The biggest mistake with TFSAs

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:01.860
is treating them like high interest savings vehicles

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:04.400
instead of long-term compounding accounts.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:08.000
Instead, always allocate the highest growth assets

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.960
that you can tolerate to the TFSA first,

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.440
then use non-registered accounts

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:14.960
for income-heavy holdings

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.920
that generate taxable distributions.

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:19.860
Open your TFSA holdings list.

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:23.100
Identify any US listed stock paying dividends

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:25.980
and calculate the 15% withholding tax

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:28.640
you would have paid on the most recent distribution.

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:33.280
Move that position into a Canadian listed ETF equivalent

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:35.440
before the next X dividend date.

